From 2642db398864d12849d0eebf44c8427b88f7fa99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(web-scan): re-verify RPC-failed router claims once;
 window head follows the latest page

Qodo on #70:
- A router claim whose check threw (transport error, or the block changed
  mid-check) on a final page was passed by the saved checkpoint and never
  re-verified. verifyClaimedPayment now marks those results `retryable`
  (also when only the second provider failed); runScan flags the match
  `recheck`, and persistable() holds the checkpoint at such a claim when it
  lies strictly after the run start. A claim at the run start was already
  retried, so it is passed: one retry per claim, the scan always moves
  forward and a claim built to always throw cannot pin the checkpoint.
- reachableHead now tracks the latest page's head instead of the highest
  seen, so a provider head that falls between pages no longer marks a
  completed scan partial or shifts its privacy windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
